# Performance & Memory

When creating effects, listeners, timers, animations, or GPU/audio resources:

- Apply engineering foundations first (always-applied rule).
- Load `skills/code/quality/performance/SKILL.md` for cleanup and optimization patterns.
- Load its `references/` only when the skill directs.

Key rules: every effect that allocates a resource returns a cleanup that frees it; close AudioContext; dispose Three.js geom/mat/textures; remove listeners and clear timers; abort in-flight fetches; no allocation in the render loop; optimize renders only where it matters.
